Introduction to AI and Machine Learning:
- Systems which perform tasks which require human intelligence
- Tasks include problem solving, natural language understanding, pattern recognition and decision making
- Examples - Calculators, voice assistance like siri or alexa, self driving cars, recognition of object by picture, chatbots providing customer services

Approchaes of AI:
  - Rule based systems - predefined rules with if and else scenarios
  - Machine learning - advanced rules with historic data, patterns and relationships

Machine Learning:
 - Used to achive artificial intelligence
 - Machine learn themselves based on data given
 - Based in data, it will identify patterns and relationships and then make decisions or predictions
 - Deep Learning used artificial neural networks learn the system
 - Examples: Filtering spam emails, promotionsl emails, recommendations in netflix, suggestions in facebook, youtube, advertizement based on search history
 - The system is flexible, scalable and has less interpretability and high data set required
 - Famous ML Models based on AI-  ChatGPT, Gemini, Copilot - Lots of data feeded to these systems
 - Types of ML - Supervised learning(Labeled data with mapped input and output), Unsupervized Learning(Unlabeled data - predicts based on patterns and relationships) and reinforcement learning(learns by interacting with environment by receiving rewards or penalties
    like online games)


Early Testing Strategies in ML Testing models(Supervised Learning)

Machine Learning Model Life cycle stages with online and offline modes

Data Preparation - > Model Enginieering - > Model Evaluation ( These 3 stages are called offline operation )

Model Deployment - > Operations - > Monitor and Evaluate - > Plan < - Business and data undestanding (This beloings to online mode and plan is linked back to data preparation)

In Model evaluation phase testing comes into picture but starts in model engineering phase

input - > ML Model - > Output
Training Data - Train the machine learning model with valid input data to train the system
Validated Data - Evaluate the machine learning learns based on data if data sufficient, overloaded, is answer accurate based on data, how much data required to get accurate answers
In validation data we provide input data only and output is checked where as in training data both input and output is given as valid data

In validation data two problems may arise - one is overfitting and other underfitting

 
Underfitting - Data will not work based on unseen data (1St iteration)
Good/Robust fit - If data gives accurate result 
Overfitting - Performance goes down due to increased data and wroks well with trained data and fails with real time data

Example:
Predicting house price
problem definition: predicting the price of house based on various features like size, number of bedrooms, age of property, location
Features(Inputs) - > Size of house in sq feet, number of bed rooms, age of house in years
Output Label (Targets) - Price of house in dollars
Training data example: Size of house in sq feet, number of bed rooms, age of house in years added for several houses
Model Training: Linear regression data is used to learn the relationship between input features and targets

Feature Selection - Data processing - Model intitialization by Choose algorithm - Model Training - Evaluation 

Evalution of supervised data: 
Training data accuracy around 95% and test data accuracy around 60%

